#!/usr/bin/env python3
import json,csv,gzip
from pathlib import Path
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];S=R.parents[1]
s=json.load(open(R/'county-sensitivity.json'));k=json.load(open(R/'known-native-order.json'));p=s['2024-president'];rows=list(csv.DictReader(open(S/'data/county-turnout.csv')));names={x['fips']:x['county'] for x in rows};coverage=json.load(open(R/'coverage.json'));controls=json.load(open(R/'extracts/certificate-controls.json'));headers=json.load(open(R/'extracts/certificate-headers.json'));candidates={x['contest']:x['candidates_display_transcription'] for x in headers};portfolio=json.load(open(R/'extracts/portfolio.json'));numpages=sum(x['pages'] for x in portfolio if x['role'].startswith('2024 county recap:'));units=[json.loads(z) for z in gzip.decompress((R/'native-units.jsonl.gz').read_bytes()).decode().splitlines()]
pct=lambda a,b:f'{100*a/b:.10f}%'
urls={2024:'https://elect.ky.gov/results/2020-2029/Documents/2024%20General%20Election%20Certification%20as%20Amended%20on%20December%209th%202024.pdf',2022:'https://elect.ky.gov/results/2020-2029/Documents/2022%20General%20Election%20results.pdf',2020:'https://elect.ky.gov/results/2020-2029/Documents/2020%20General%20Election%20Results.pdf'}
archives={2024:'20241223120817',2022:'20221223031129',2020:'20201120170339'}
source=lambda y:f'[{y} state certificate]({urls[y]}) ([exact archived original](https://web.archive.org/web/{archives[y]}id_/{urls[y]}))'
text=f'''# Kentucky turnout and source-native reporting geography

Research completed from public original evidence captured through **2026-10-20 UTC**. **A complete statewide native presidential ordering is unavailable.** The [dispatch contract](data/turnout/priority-set.json) keeps canonical native total/order/top15/min80/priority/remainder **null** and ordered priority/dispatch keys **empty**. The complete120-county calculation below is a **county sensitivity**, with its own denominator; it does not substitute for precincts, wards, combined groups, ballot styles, or central administrative/method units. Peer existence is verified by the coordinator's session message; independent numerical agreement and coordinator acceptance remain pending.

The primary historical contest is **2024 President and Vice President**, because Kentucky had no2024 Senate general election. **2020 McConnell–McGrath** is the same ClassII Senate seat; **2022 Paul–Booker** is the separate ClassIII Senate midterm comparator. Each uses all reported candidate/named-write-in columns. Candidate votes, ballots cast, voter-history participation, and dated registration are separate measurements. The sources are {source(2024)}, {source(2022)}, and {source(2020)}; full individual receipts and exact raw/stored byte pins are in the [source registry](data/turnout/source/entities.json).

**Original-first evidence.** Before opening any coordinator numerical diagnostic/parser/table or peer derivative, this worker independently read original certificate bodies, extracted every120-county candidate position and printed footer, captured every linked2024 county recap, and retained native/method/admin/null/source-position contexts. [First immutable witness](data/turnout/history/original-first/witness.json), SHA256 `a101f4693c6cbf1ab0f1f0a5872a26037bbe24eb43f2d30760f3861d63afdafe`, and [complete addendum](data/turnout/history/original-first-v2/witness.json), SHA256 `04944536c174c7eef726789370114aabb7d553bc5b96784921b8a7cd42a8d747`, contain immutable script/extraction/receipt bodies and exact raw-source references. [Third original-first witness](data/turnout/history/original-first-v3/witness.json), SHA256 `cf42c9f312acbab43f7f4d3c52a68a47daa1648b7470e0f3406ecc978f7f4b45`, freezes the source-only correction after the offline checker found Madison's wrapped Kennedy numeric row. The [complete prior owned body witness](data/turnout/history/before-native-continuation-repair/witness.json) precedes that narrow repair. The qualified captured-native total increased by436 from restoring the full original row; no certificate or source byte changed. No peer count was used to repair an original source. Failed parsers, full prior output bodies, source-linked inputs and errors are retained in [history](data/turnout/history/). Later additions are owned original-source calculation/control/report work, not external numerical imports.

**County sensitivity result.** The descending top15 are **{', '.join(names[q] for q in p['top15']['keys'])}**. They supply **{p['top15']['votes']:,}/{p['denominator']:,} = {pct(p['top15']['votes'],p['denominator'])}**. The minimum descending county set reaching80% contains **{p['min80']['count']} counties**, **{p['min80']['votes']:,} votes = {pct(p['min80']['votes'],p['denominator'])}**. The preceding49 contain **{p['min80']['preceding_votes']:,} = {pct(p['min80']['preceding_votes'],p['denominator'])}**; **{names[p['min80']['crossing_key']]} ({p['min80']['crossing_votes']:,})** crosses. The remaining70 contain **{p['remainder']['votes']:,}** votes. Integer comparisons use `5*cumulative >= 4*denominator`; descending largest-first proves49 cannot reach80%. Ties use the complete source key/FIPS. These are computed directly from the {source(2024)}; every county outside the sensitivity priority remains in the denominator.

The ordered county sensitivity50 is: **{', '.join(names[q] for q in p['priority_keys'])}**. The [complete county sensitivity JSON](data/turnout/county-sensitivity.json) retains every full order, ordered priority and remainder for all three contests and each separate volume/registration measure. The compatibility [county-turnout.csv](data/county-turnout.csv) has120 county-parent rows, all29 candidate columns, source scopes, exact shares/cumulatives and explicit canonical nulls. Its filename does not authorize any native-unit substitution.

**Candidate controls and tickets.** Every county sum equals its independently extracted printed statewide candidate footer:3,480 county candidate cells and29 controls. Presidential running mates share one vote column and are not counted again. Named Write-In labels are source ballot identities, not ordinary party affiliations; no generic pool is manufactured from missing named columns. Complete raw positioned headers, including spacing/case defects, and explicitly marked display transcriptions are retained in [headers](data/turnout/extracts/certificate-headers.json); every raw token has page, line, character span and full source row in [fields](data/turnout/extracts/certificate-fields.json). All selected first/final table pages were rendered and visually inspected; other county glyphs use the original text layer, not a claim of manual reading of every cell. Poppler's flate warnings are retained without modifying original PDFs.

| Contest / candidate (running mate where applicable) | Party / source label | County sum = printed footer |
| --- | --- | ---: |
'''
for contest in ['2024-president','2022-senate','2020-senate']:
 for z in [q for q in controls if q['contest']==contest]:
  name=z['candidate']+(f" / {z['running_mate']}" if z['running_mate'] else '')
  text+=f"| {contest}: {name} | {z['party_or_ballot_label']} | {z['value']:,} |\n"
